# Edge vhost for morrowind.virtastic.app — deployed as a drop-in into the shared edge Caddy's
# sites dir (on the VPS: /opt/edge/sites/morrowind.caddy; imported by /opt/edge/Caddyfile via
# `import sites/*.caddy`). The shared edge terminates TLS with the Cloudflare Origin cert and
# reverse-proxies to the morrowind container by name on the shared docker network.
#
# The container's own Caddy already sets COOP/COEP/CORP (required for SharedArrayBuffer) and serves
# precompressed .br + honors Range; those response headers pass through this reverse_proxy. So this
# vhost deliberately does NOT set them again (duplicate COOP/COEP breaks crossOriginIsolated) and
# does NOT `encode` (would double-encode the pre-br'd assets / interfere with Range). No `import
# inject` either — morrowind is greenfield with no x-from-cloudflare origin guard.
morrowind.virtastic.app {
	tls /certs/virtastic.crt /certs/virtastic.key
	import sec_headers
	reverse_proxy morrowind:8080
}
